                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Short gametime, but none of it grabbed me ... maybe the game plays better in VR, which I don't have.\r\n\r\nFrom what I played, it's all about tile placement and minor interaction with the humans in the world.  Place forests to give them access to wood so they can advance their society ... place stone (not a stone tile, but stone on an existing tile) and you give them access to stone so they can advance their society (and so forth).\r\n\r\nIt wasn't clear why I couldn't do certain things ... like 'magical plain' or 'magical forest' ... they had mana costs but couldn't be placed as tiles (just like stone they have to be added to an existing tile), but no tile I placed (I had access to temperate, arctic, and desert tiles by this point) 'allowed' those magical add ons.\r\n\r\nIt's an interesting thing to look at (I hesitate at calling it a game), but no strong hook in the early gameplay for me.",
